title: 'pallet-vesting: migrate from LockableCurrency to fungible freezes'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    Migrates `pallet-vesting` off the deprecated `Currency`/`LockableCurrency` traits onto the
    `fungible` trait family. The unvested balance is now held with a `fungible` freeze under
    `FreezeReason::Vesting`, and transfers/balance reads use the `fungible` traits. Part of
    #12399 / #226.

    Config changes (breaking):
    - `Currency: LockableCurrency` is replaced by `Currency: fungible::{Inspect, Mutate,
      MutateFreeze}` plus a new `RuntimeFreezeReason` and a `FreezeReason::Vesting` hold reason.
    - `OldCurrency: LockableCurrency` is added, kept solely so the legacy vesting lock can be
      removed during the lazy migration. It can be removed once all locks have been migrated.
    - The `UnvestedFundsAllowedWithdrawReasons` config item is removed (see the behavior change
      below).

    Pre-existing vesting locks are migrated lazily: any account's legacy lock is converted to a
    freeze the first time it interacts with the pallet (`vest`, `vested_transfer`, etc.), and a
    permissionless `migrate_to_freeze` extrinsic is provided to convert an account on demand.

    Behavior change - `UnvestedFundsAllowedWithdrawReasons` is removed:
    The old `LockableCurrency` lock was created with a `WithdrawReasons` bitmask
    (`WithdrawReasons::except(UnvestedFundsAllowedWithdrawReasons::get())`), which let the
    operations named in `UnvestedFundsAllowedWithdrawReasons` draw from the still-locked
    (unvested) balance. `fungible` freezes have no equivalent carve-out concept: a freeze
    unconditionally prevents the balance from dropping below the frozen amount. Consequently,
    operations that were previously permitted to spend from the unvested balance via those
    withdraw-reason exceptions can no longer do so. Runtimes that configured a non-default
    `UnvestedFundsAllowedWithdrawReasons` should review this change, as it tightens what the
    unvested balance can be used for. The in-tree runtimes all used the default
    (`WithdrawReasons::except(TRANSFER | RESERVE)`).
crates:
- name: pallet-vesting
  bump: major
- name: pallet-vesting-precompiles
  bump: patch
- name: rococo-runtime
  bump: major
- name: westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: major
- name: polkadot-runtime-common
  bump: none
